The '''2022 Halton Borough Council election''' took place on 5 May 2022, alongside [[2022 United Kingdom local elections|other local elections in the United Kingdom]], to elect a third of [[Halton Borough Council|the council's]] 54 seats. The [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party]] won most of the 18 seats up for election, comfortably retaining their overall majority. Only one seat switched hands: Daresbury, Moore and Sandymoor elected a [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative]], a loss for the [[Green Party of England and Wales|Green Party]] who were left without any members on the council.

